# pool_edge -- a bullnose coping ring round the Oval. Placed in island.txt at the pool's own
# centre and at the deck's top, so these are local coordinates about the middle of the water.
#
# The pool is an ellipse, and a 1 m coping run is straight, so the ring is twenty chords: each
# run is scaled to its own chord and turned so its rounded edge faces the water. Twenty is where
# the faceting stops reading as facets from the deck. They all share one mesh and one texture, so
# the whole ring is a single instanced draw.
piece models/own/arch/pool_coping_run.obj    9.268  0.000   0.927   2.026 1.000 1.000   84.3 0.0 0.0   1.77 1.96 2.26  tex paving_stone 0.8
